## 🔑 How Authentication Works

### 1. Registration

The user enters their:

* Name
* Email
* Password

The information is stored in the browser's **LocalStorage**.

### 2. Login

The user enters their email and password.

JavaScript checks the entered credentials against the registered user data stored in LocalStorage.

If the credentials are correct, the user is redirected to the dashboard.

```javascript
window.location.href = "dashboard.html";
```

### 3. Protected Dashboard

The dashboard checks whether a user is logged in.

```javascript
const loggedInUser = localStorage.getItem("loggedInUser");

if (!loggedInUser) {
    window.location.href = "login.html";
}
```

If there is no logged-in user, the dashboard redirects the user back to the login page.

### 4. Welcome Message

The logged-in user's name can be displayed on the dashboard.

```javascript
const loggedInUser = JSON.parse(
    localStorage.getItem("loggedInUser")
);

document.getElementById("username").textContent =
    loggedInUser.name;
```

Example:

```text
Welcome, Shivam 👋
```

### 5. Logout

When the user clicks the logout button, the login information is removed from LocalStorage.

```javascript
localStorage.removeItem("loggedInUser");

window.location.href = "login.html";
```

## 🎯 Project Flow

```text
Register
   ↓
Store User Data
   ↓
Login
   ↓
Validate Credentials
   ↓
Login Successful
   ↓
Dashboard
   ↓
Display Username
   ↓
Logout
   ↓
Login Page
```

